.TH SDL_CreateWindowWithProperties 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_CreateWindowWithProperties \- Create a window with the specified properties.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_video.h>
.PP
.BI "SDL_Window * SDL_CreateWindowWithProperties(SDL_PropertiesID props);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The window size is a request and may be different than expected based on the desktop layout and window manager policies\[char46] Your application should be prepared to handle a window of any size\[char46]
.PP
These are the supported properties:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_ALWAYS_ON_TOP_BOOLEAN :
true if the window should be always on top
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_BORDERLESS_BOOLEAN :
true if the window has no window decoration
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_CONSTRAIN_POPUP_BOOLEAN :
true if the \(dqtooltip\(dq and \(dqmenu\(dq window types should be automatically constrained to be entirely within display bounds (default), false if no constraints on the position are desired\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_EXTERNAL_GRAPHICS_CONTEXT_BOOLEAN :
true if the window will be used with an externally managed graphics context\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_FOCUSABLE_BOOLEAN :
true if the window should accept keyboard input (defaults true)
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_FULLSCREEN_BOOLEAN :
true if the window should start in fullscreen mode at desktop resolution
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_HEIGHT_NUMBER :
the height of the window
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_HIDDEN_BOOLEAN :
true if the window should start hidden
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_HIGH_PIXEL_DENSITY_BOOLEAN :
true if the window uses a high pixel density buffer if possible
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_MAXIMIZED_BOOLEAN :
true if the window should start maximized
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_MENU_BOOLEAN :
true if the window is a popup menu
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_METAL_BOOLEAN :
true if the window will be used with Metal rendering
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_MINIMIZED_BOOLEAN :
true if the window should start minimized
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_MODAL_BOOLEAN :
true if the window is modal to its parent
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_MOUSE_GRABBED_BOOLEAN :
true if the window starts with grabbed mouse focus
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_OPENGL_BOOLEAN :
true if the window will be used with OpenGL rendering
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_PARENT_POINTER :
an
.BR SDL_Window
that will be the parent of this window, required for windows with the \(dqtooltip\(dq, \(dqmenu\(dq, and \(dqmodal\(dq properties
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_RESIZABLE_BOOLEAN :
true if the window should be resizable
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_TITLE_STRING :
the title of the window, in UTF-8 encoding
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_TRANSPARENT_BOOLEAN :
true if the window show transparent in the areas with alpha of 0
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_TOOLTIP_BOOLEAN :
true if the window is a tooltip
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_UTILITY_BOOLEAN :
true if the window is a utility window, not showing in the task bar and window list
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_VULKAN_BOOLEAN :
true if the window will be used with Vulkan rendering
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_WIDTH_NUMBER :
the width of the window
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_X_NUMBER :
the x position of the window, or
.BR SDL_WINDOWPOS_CENTERED ,
defaults to
.BR SDL_WINDOWPOS_UNDEFINED \[char46]
This is relative to the parent for windows with the \(dqtooltip\(dq or \(dqmenu\(dq property set\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_Y_NUMBER :
the y position of the window, or
.BR SDL_WINDOWPOS_CENTERED ,
defaults to
.BR SDL_WINDOWPOS_UNDEFINED \[char46]
This is relative to the parent for windows with the \(dqtooltip\(dq or \(dqmenu\(dq property set\[char46]
.PP
These are additional supported properties on macOS:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_COCOA_WINDOW_POINTER :
the
.BR (__unsafe_unretained)
NSWindow associated with the window, if you want to wrap an existing window\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_COCOA_VIEW_POINTER :
the
.BR (__unsafe_unretained)
NSView associated with the window, defaults to
.BR "[window contentView]"
.PP
These are additional supported properties on iOS, tvOS, and visionOS:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_WINDOWSCENE_POINTER :
the
.BR (__unsafe_unretained)
UIWindowScene associated with the window, defaults to the active window scene\[char46]
.PP
These are additional supported properties on Wayland:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_WAYLAND_SURFACE_ROLE_CUSTOM_BOOLEAN
- true if the application wants to use the Wayland surface for a custom role and does not want it attached to an XDG toplevel window\[char46] See [README-wayland](README-wayland) for more information on using custom surfaces\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_WAYLAND_CREATE_EGL_WINDOW_BOOLEAN
- true if the application wants an associated
.BR wl_egl_window
object to be created and attached to the window, even if the window does not have the OpenGL property or
.BR SDL_WINDOW_OPENGL
flag set\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_WAYLAND_WINDOW_ID_STRING
- a string used as a stable identifier for toplevel windows for the purpose of allowing the compositor to save/restore their state between runs\[char46] This should be human readable, but not translated, and must be unique for each individual window\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_WAYLAND_WL_SURFACE_POINTER
- the wl_surface associated with the window, if you want to wrap an existing window\[char46] See [README-wayland](README-wayland) for more information\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_WAYLAND_ENABLE_INSETS_BOOLEAN
- true if the application wants to enable custom border inset window properties\[char46] See [README-wayland](README-wayland) for more information\[char46]
.PP
These are additional supported properties on Windows:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_WIN32_HWND_POINTER :
the HWND associated with the window, if you want to wrap an existing window\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_WIN32_PIXEL_FORMAT_HWND_POINTER :
optional, another window to share pixel format with, useful for OpenGL windows
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_WIN32_STYLE_EX_NUMBER :
the window style (WS_EX_*) flags to use instead of the defaults\[char46]
.PP
These are additional supported properties with X11:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_X11_WINDOW_NUMBER :
the X11 Window associated with the window, if you want to wrap an existing window\[char46]
.PP
The window is implicitly shown if the \(dqhidden\(dq property is not set\[char46]
.PP
These are additional supported properties with Emscripten:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_EMSCRIPTEN_CANVAS_ID_STRING :
the id given to the canvas element\[char46] This should start with a \(aq#\(aq sign
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_EMSCRIPTEN_KEYBOARD_ELEMENT_STRING :
override the binding element for keyboard inputs for this canvas\[char46] The variable can be one of:
.PP
\(bu \(dq#window\(dq: the javascript window object (default)
.PP
\(bu \(dq#document\(dq: the javascript document object
.PP
\(bu \(dq#screen\(dq: the javascript window\[char46]screen object
.PP
\(bu \(dq#canvas\(dq: the WebGL canvas element
.PP
\(bu \(dq#none\(dq: Don\(aqt bind anything at all
.PP
\(bu any other string without a leading # sign applies to the element on the page with that ID\[char46] Windows with the \(dqtooltip\(dq and \(dqmenu\(dq properties are popup windows and have the behaviors and guidelines outlined in
.BR SDL_CreatePopupWindow ()\[char46]
.PP
These are additional supported properties with visionOS:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_VISIONOS_SETTINGS_STRING :
the settings of the window in JSON format\[char46] If this isn\(aqt set, the window will have standard UIKit behavior\[char46] If this is set to \(dq\(dq or a valid setting string then the window is created with enhanced features allowing curved display\[char46] The curvature in the settings is defined as a radius in millimeters\[char46] A common value for a gaming monitor is 1000 and a setting string for that would be \(dq{\(rs\(dqcurvatureRadius\(rs\(dq:1000}\(dq\[char46]
.PP
If this window is being created to be used with an
.BR SDL_Renderer ,
you should not add a graphics API specific property
.BR "" ( SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_OPENGL_BOOLEAN ,
etc), as SDL will handle that internally when it chooses a renderer\[char46] However, SDL might need to recreate your window at that point, which may cause the window to appear briefly, and then flicker as it is recreated\[char46] The correct approach to this is to create the window with the
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_HIDDEN_BOOLEAN
property set to true, then create the renderer, then show the window with
.BR SDL_ShowWindow ()\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I props
the properties to use\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the window that was created or NULL on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
This function should only be called on the main thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_CreateProperties (3),
.BR SDL_CreateWindow (3),
.BR SDL_DestroyWindow (3)
